article.common-document
  header.header
    h2.title JoGo dataset
  .contents
    section.section
      h3.sectiontitle Summary
      p.body
        a.hyper-text.-external(target='_blank', href='https://jogo.csml.org/') JoGo (Joint Open Genome and Omics)
        | is a human haplotype database based on long-read whole-genome sequencing. TogoVar includes JoGo-derived
        | variant frequencies as a search target and provides links from variant reports to related JoGo information.
      ul.unordered-list
        li Version: JoGo 1.0
        li Participants: 258 individuals from five continents
        li Analysis method: long-read whole-genome sequencing
        li Number of genes: 19,194
        li Number of haplotypes: 4,656,478
        li Reference genomes: GRCh38 and CHM13v2

    section.section
      h3.sectiontitle ACTG hierarchical nomenclature
      p.body
        | JoGo represents haplotypes at four levels: A (amino acid), C (coding sequence), T (transcript and UTR),
        | and G (gene body). This ACTG hierarchical nomenclature makes it possible to compare complete gene sequence
        | patterns in addition to individual variants.

